# Behavioral Economics and Healthy Behaviors : Key Concepts and Current Research

**Authors:** Yaniv Hanoch, Andrew C. Barnes, T. Rice

## Abstract
In the collection Behavioral Economics and Healthy Behaviors: Key Concepts and Current Research, edited by Yaniv Hanoch, Andrew J. Barnes and Thomas Rice, contributors explore a number of health-related areas where behavioural economics can be used, from health behaviours to health care and policy. This volume does a good job of discussing the ‘behavioural’ aspects of behavioural economics and considering its potential applications, writes Joan Costa-Font, though he would have welcomed more discussion of its limitations too.

